        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "ea6ffa04-f3ce-57ef-9a1e-a5f62c7ab859",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, Gerry Griffin, Ed Harris\n- Works: Failure Is Not an Option, Apollo 13\n- Organizations: NASA\n- Roles: Flight Director, Mission Control team\n- Programs: Gemini program, Apollo program, Apollo 11\n\nFacts:\n- Failure Is Not an Option was produced in 2003.\n- Failure Is Not an Option includes speakers Chris Kraft, Gene Kranz, Jim Lovell, Jerry Bostick, Ed Fendell, Gene Cernan, John Llewellen, John Aaron, Glynn Lunney, Wally Schirra, and Gerry Griffin.\n- Gene Kranz served as a NASA Flight Director during the Gemini and Apollo programs and succeeded NASA founding Flight Director Chris Kraft in that role.\n- Gene Kranz served as flight director during Apollo 11, the first lunar landing.\n- Gene Kranz is best known for directing the Mission Control team efforts that saved the Apollo 13 crew.\n- Apollo 13 later became the subject of a major motion picture in which Ed Harris portrayed Gene Kranz.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
